# The SHA-256 of the certificate that signs every Anshin APK on GitHub Releases, as `apksigner verify --print-certs`
# prints it ("certificate SHA-256 digest"): one line of 64 lowercase hex characters below these comments.
# scripts/apk-sign.sh and scripts/apk-verify.sh refuse any other certificate, so the Release workflow cannot publish
# an APK signed with a swapped key. It changes only when the key itself does, in a reviewed pull request: see
# docs/maintaining.md, The APK signing key.
